Article 8 (Delegation of Authority)
The Committee shall delegate the following powers to its Chairperson under Article 61 of the Act: [Amended on April 5, 2011.]
1. Recommending selection of a representative under Article 15 (2) of the Act;
2. Granting permission for succession to status under Article 16 (7) of the Act;
3. Deciding on correction of a respondent under Article 17 (2) and (5) of the Act;
4. Permitting appointment of an agent under Article 18 (1) 5 of the Act;
5. Permitting intervention in an appeal under Article 20 (5) of the Act;
6. Requesting intervention in an appeal under Article 21 (1) of the Act;
7. Permitting amendment of the purport or grounds of a claim under Article 29 (6) of the Act;
8. Requiring correction of defects and making corrections ex officio under Article 32 (1) of the Act;
9. Permitting oral hearings under Article 40 (2) of the Act.
